export const str REGISTRY_SRC =
    "# CobaltC Diagnostic Registry\n\nStatus: normative artifact\nVersion: 1.77.0\nConforms to: `spec/02-sche"
    "ma.md` (Kind: Diagnostic, `diag.<name>`)\nGoverned by: `CobaltC_Master_Instructions.md` §19\n\n## Purp"
    "ose\n\nEvery `diag.*` id any rule produces, with the fields §19 requires.\nEvery entry has **Status:**"
    " ACCEPTED. Conventions: **Phase** is\n*static* (a `disposition: rejected` rule, or a `checked` rule w"
    "hose\nguard `rule.control.flow-analysis` refuted), *dynamic* (a `checked`\nrule's runtime guard), or *"
    "both*. **Summary** is the diagnostic's\nmessage when its occurrence gives none of its own. **Location"
    "** is,\nunless stated, the expression the triggering rule's premises were\nevaluated against; it is a "
    "file, a line and a column, the column being\nthat of the location's first token, counted in character"
    "s from 1 (a\nlocation that is a declaration or a statement is its first token).\n**Related** cites `ex"
    ".*` (`spec/examples.md`). When a program has\nseveral static errors, the one reported first is the fi"
    "rst in the source (the\nlowest line; among one line's errors, any), whatever order a checker\nvisits t"
    "he program in (`CHG-0130`). D-0321: the others follow it, in source\norder, a blank line between, the"
    "n a line `N errors` (`N errors; the first 10\nare shown` past ten): the checks run in phases (the tex"
    "t's syntax, then names,\nthen each declaration, then the bodies' types and the static pass, then the\n"
    "static assertions), a later phase only when the earlier found nothing, and a\nphase reports at most o"
    "ne error for each item (a function or a declaration),\nits earliest; a syntax error ends its item, an"
    "d the text is read again from\nthe next one, unless its brackets do not balance. D-0323: within the p"
    "hase of\nthe bodies, a body reports the earliest error of each of its own block's\nstatements (and its"
    " tail) that stands on its own: a statement that mentions a\nlocal a failed statement declared without"
    " a written type, or left unknown\n(not valid and initialised before it, known from a literal, or hold"
    "ing a\nreference), is not checked, and after a failed `return`, `break`, `continue`,\n`exit` or `fault"
    "` the rest of the block is not; a local a failed statement\ndeclares with a written type has that typ"
    "e. The blocks of a statement in\nstatement position (an `if`, a loop, a `match`, a block) are checked"
    " the same\nway, except that a failed statement ends its block, as a `return` would, and\nthe statement"
    " that holds the block is then a failed statement itself. When a statement was not checked,\nthe repor"
    "t ends with the line `note: statements that depend on a failed\nstatement were not checked`. A confor"
    "mance case requires the first diagnostic\nonly.\n\n**How a diagnostic is shown** (D-0228). Both impleme"
    "ntations print every\ndiagnostic in the same form, byte for byte. By default it is short: a first\nlin"
    "e `error[diag.x]: message` for a static diagnostic or `fault[diag.x]:\nmessage` for a dynamic one, wh"
    "ere the message is the occurrence's own or\nthe entry's **Summary**; then `--> file:line:column`; the"
    "n the source line,\nread from the file when the diagnostic is shown, with carets under the\nlocation's"
    " token; then `= repair:` and the entry's **Repair**. A file\nthat cannot be read is shown as its loca"
    "tion alone. With `--explain`\n(both tools), or with `COBALTC_EXPLAIN` set to anything but empty or `0"
    "`\n(this is how a compiled program is asked), the entry's Rule, Invariant,\nRequired, Observed and Pro"
    "venance follow, then its Related examples and\nthis registry. A conformance case requires the id and "
    "the phase\n(`spec/conformance.md`), which a runner reads from the first line's\nopening `error[diag.ID"
    "]` or `fault[diag.ID]` (`impl/conformance/run.py`);\nthe location is as this registry gives it; the r"
    "est of the form's\nwording is not normative.\nA dynamic diagnostic is located by its line (the two imp"
    "lementations check\nsome operations of one statement at different sub-expressions); its caret is\nunde"
    "r the line's first token, or, where the fault names its operation and the\nline has that operation on"
    "ce, under it: the operator of `diag.arith-overflow`,\nthe indexed name of `diag.index-out-of-bounds` "
    "(report 252).\n\n## Syntax\n\n- `diag.syntax-error` — Summary: the text is not a CobaltC program here."
    " Phase: static. Rule: the grammar, `spec/22` (lexical §1, syntactic §2–§3, and each rule that m"
    "akes a form a syntax error, such as `[Slice-Not-Borrowed]`). Invariant: none. Required: the text is "
    "a CobaltC program by the grammar. Observed: at the location, the first token (or character) where th"
    "e grammar allows none of what the message says was expected; nothing of the program runs. Provenance"
    ": the source text. Repair: correct the text there; the message names what was expected and what was "
    "found. Location: that token.\n\n## Names and scoping\n\n- `diag.slice-of-whole` — Summary: a warning o"
    "f `--check`: `&x[0..$]` (or `&mut x[0..$]`) at a position whose declared type is a slice or a `Strin"
    "gView`, where `[Coerce-Slice]` or `[Coerce-Text]` makes the plain borrow, the view, the slice or the"
    " reference the same thing. Phase: static (a warning; the program is accepted). Rule: `rule.type.coer"
    "ce-slice`, `rule.type.coerce-text` (`spec/12`, D-0312 §3.2). Invariant: none. Required: nothing; `["
    "lo..hi]` is for a part. Observed: a slice from `0` to `$` of a `Vec`, an array or a `String` place, "
    "of a view, a slice or a `str` value, or of what a reference refers to, where the position declares a"
    " slice or a `StringView`. Provenance: the slice. Repair: write `&x` (`&mut x`); a view, a slice, a `"
    "str` or a reference as it is. Location: the slice, with its column.\n- `diag.text-copy-literal` — S"
    "ummary: a warning of `--check`: `String::copy(\"…\")` where a `String` is declared. Phase: static (a"
    " warning; the program is accepted). Rule: `rule.type.coerce-text` `[Coerce-Text]` (`spec/12`, D-0312"
    " §4). Invariant: none. Required: nothing; the literal is already the `String` there. Observed: `Str"
    "ing::copy` of a literal at a position whose expected type is `String`. Provenance: the call. Repair:"
    " write the literal. Location: the literal.\n- `diag.text-copy-whole` — Summary: a warning of `--che"
    "ck`: `String::copy(&s)` of a whole `String`. Phase: static (a warning; the program is accepted). Rul"
    "e: `rule.type.coerce-text` `[Coerce-Text]` (`spec/12`, D-0312 §4). Invariant: none. Required: nothi"
    "ng; the copy is right. Observed: `String::copy(&s)` with `s` a `String` place. Provenance: the call."
    " Repair: write `String::clone(&s)`, which says a whole `String` is copied. Location: the argument.\n-"
    " `diag.no-effect` — Summary: a warning of `--check`: an expression statement whose value is its on"
    "ly effect (a comparison, a name, a field or a literal). Phase: static (a warning; the program is acc"
    "epted). Rule: `rule.expr.seq` (`spec/13` §3, D-0336). Invariant: none. Required: nothing; the state"
    "ment does nothing. Observed: `count == count + 1;`, `x < 3;`, `x;`, `p.f;`, `3;` as a statement (a c"
    "all may have effects and arithmetic may fault, so neither is one). Provenance: the statement. Repair"
    ": assign with `=`, or discard a value on purpose with `_ = …;`. Location: the statement.\n- `diag.h"
    "andle-discarded` — Summary: a warning of `--check`: `_ = spawn(…);` (or `_ =` of any `handle<T>`"
    "), or a `spawn(…);` statement (report 350), whose handle ends at once and so joins its thread on t"
    "hat line. Phase: static (a warning; the program is accepted). Rule: `rule.conc.join` `[Handle-Destru"
    "ctor]` (`spec/19` §1, report 302). Invariant: none. Required: nothing; the statement runs the threa"
    "d to its end before the next. Observed: `_ = spawn(work, x);`, which reads as \"start it and go on\" ("
    "Rust's `let _ = thread::spawn(…)` detaches). Provenance: the statement. Repair: keep the handle (`"
    "handle<T> h = spawn(…);`, or push it onto a `Vec` of handles) and `join` it where the work must be"
    " done. Location: the statement.\n- `diag.comparison-constant` — Summary: a warning of `--check`: a "
    "comparison of an unsigned value with `0` that cannot be false (`i >= 0`, `0 <= i`) or cannot be true"
    " (`i < 0`, `0 > i`). Phase: static (a warning; the program is accepted). Rule: `rule.arith.cmp` (`sp"
    "ec/06`, D-0336). Invariant: none. Required: nothing; the comparison has one result. Observed: `>=`/`"
    "<` against `0` of an operand of an unsigned type, not one whose type is a type parameter's in a gene"
    "ric body's instantiation. Provenance: the comparison. Repair: count down with `while (i > 0) { i -= "
    "1; … }`, or count up and index from the end; for `a - b >= 0`, compare `a >= b` (the subtraction f"
    "aults when `b > a`). Location: the comparison.\n- `diag.match-arm-break` — Summary: a warning of `-"
    "-check`: `break;` as the last statement of a `match` arm's block inside a loop, which leaves the loo"
    "p (C's `switch` habit). Phase: static (a warning; the program is accepted). Rule: `rule.control.whil"
    "e` (`spec/14`, D-0337). Invariant: none. Required: nothing; the `break` leaves the enclosing loop, a"
    "s written. Observed: an arm `p : { s; …; break; }` (a statement before the `break;`) of a `match` "
    "inside a `while`, `for` or `foreach`, whose pattern `p` is a literal (a variant's arm, `None : { …"
    "; break; }`, never warns). Provenance: the `break`. Repair: delete the `break` (an arm never runs on"
    " into the next); to leave the loop, write `break` as the block's value without `;` (`{ …; break }`"
    ") or as the arm's value (`p : break,`). Location: the `break`.\n- `diag.unbound-name` — Summary: th"
    "is name is not declared. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.value-object.binding-lookup` `[Binding-Lookup-Un"
    "bound]`, `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Unbound]`, `spec/21` §0 `fault`'s name (D-0083). Invariant"
    ": none. Required: the name resolves to a binding or item. Observed: it does not. Provenance: use sit"
    "e vs. every declaration in scope. Repair: declare it, fix the spelling, or add an `import` (`import "
    "std;` for the standard library, `CHG-0033`). Related: `ex.unbound-name`.\n- `diag.ambiguous-name` —"
    " Summary: this name could mean more than one item. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Reso"
    "lve-Ambiguous]`. Required: exactly one candidate. Observed: several (two `import`s, two imported mod"
    "ules exporting the name, two enums of the same module with the variant, or, where no module of the p"
    "rogram's own has it, two imported enums with it). Provenance: the candidate declarations. Repair: qu"
    "alify the name.\n- `diag.name-not-visible` — Summary: this item is private to its module. Phase: st"
    "atic. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Not-Visible]`; `rule.module.visibility` `[Field-Not-Visi"
    "ble]` (a field named by `e.f`, a struct literal, or a destructuring). Required: `visible(M', name, M"
    ")`. Observed: private. Provenance: the declaration's `export` marker vs. the use site's module. Repa"
    "ir: mark `export` or move the reference.\n- `diag.no-main` — Summary: the program has no `main` it "
    "can start from. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn.program` `[Program-No-Main]`. Invariant: none. Require"
    "d: exactly one non-generic, non-`extern` `main` at the root module, with no parameters, returning `v"
    "oid` or `u8`. Observed: none there (a `main` inside a module is the ordinary item `m::main`), or one"
    " with parameters, another return type, type parameters, or `extern`. Provenance: the root module's i"
    "tems. Repair: declare `fn main()` or `fn main() : u8` at the root (arguments come from `arg`, `spec/"
    "21` §2c), or run the file that has one — a file-backed module's body is not a program (`spec/17` "
    "§5). Location: the root `main`, if there is one; otherwise the program as a whole.\n- `diag.const-no"
    "t-constant` — Summary: a constant's value must be known before the program runs. Phase: static. Ru"
    "le: `rule.module.const` `[Const-Not-Constant]`, `[Const-Cycle]`, `[Const-Local-Not-Constant]` (`spec"
    "/17` §1a). Invariant: none. Required: a `const`'s type is not a resource, its initializer is a cons"
    "tant expression (literals, operators, other constants, struct, array and variant literals of constan"
    "t expressions and their fields and elements, a function's name, the pure intrinsics listed there), a"
    "nd no constant depends on itself; a local constant's initializer names no local variable and no type"
    " parameter of its function. Observed: one of these fails. Provenance: the `const` declaration. Repai"
    "r: use only constants in the initializer (a local variable is not one, even when set from a literal:"
    " declare it `const` too), compute the value in a function instead, or break the cycle. Location: the"
    " `const`.\n- `diag.format-invalid` — Summary: this format string is not valid. Phase: static. Rule:"
    " `rule.stdlib.format` `[Format-Invalid]` (`spec/21` §2f). Invariant: none. Required: the format of "
    "`printf`, `sprintf`, `eprintf` or `String::appendf` is a string literal whose every `%` begins a spe"
    "cifier `%[flags][width][.precision]conversion` with a conversion of `d i u x X o b f F e E g G s v` "
    "(or is `%%`), and flags the conversion takes. Observed: a format that is not a literal, a `%` at the"
    " end, an unknown conversion, a flag the conversion does not take (`%#d`, `%0s`, `%+x`, `%05v`), a pr"
    "ecision on `%v`, or a width or precision above 4096. Provenance: the call. Repair: fix the specifier"
    "; write `%%` for a `%`. Location: the call.\n- `diag.module-file-not-found` — Summary: the module's"
    " file cannot be read. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.file` `[Module-File-Missing]`. Invariant: no"
    "ne. Required: the declaration's path, resolved against the declaring file's directory, names a reada"
    "ble file. Observed: it names none. Provenance: the declaration's path and the directory it was resol"
    "ved against. Repair: fix the path or create the file. Location: the `module` declaration.\n- `diag.mo"
    "dule-cycle` — Summary: these module files contain each other. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.fi"
    "le` `[Module-File-Cycle]`. Invariant: none. Required: no file's body contains, directly or through f"
    "urther file-backed declarations, itself. Observed: a cycle `F → … → F`. Provenance: each decla"
    "ration on the cycle. Repair: break the cycle — move the shared items into a third file both name. "
    "Location: the declaration that closes the cycle.\n- `diag.module-file-duplicate` — Summary: this fi"
    "le is already declared as a module. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.file` `[Module-File-Duplicate]"
    "`. Invariant: none. Required: each file is named by at most one declaration in the program. Observed"
    ": two. Provenance: both declarations. Repair: declare the module once and reach it by qualified path"
    " or `import`. Location: the second declaration.\n- `diag.duplicate-local` — Summary: this name is a"
    "lready declared in this block. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.value-object.binding-form` `[Binding-Form-"
    "Redeclared]` (D-0131). Invariant: none. Required: each name is declared at most once in a declaratio"
    "n region — a block's statements with the parameters, loop names or pattern binder governing it. Ob"
