    "336). Provenance: both declarations. Repair: rename one, or move it into a module. Location: the sec"
    "ond declaration (for two fields, the struct).\n- `diag.foreign-associated-fn` — Summary: an associa"
    "ted function must be declared beside its type. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Assoc-Fn"
    "-Foreign-Type]`. Invariant: none. Required: `fn T::name` is declared in the module that declares the"
    " struct or enum `T`. Observed: `T` is declared elsewhere (for example `std`'s `Vec`) or not at all. "
    "Provenance: the declaration and `T`'s module. Repair: declare an ordinary function, or move the decl"
    "aration into `T`'s module. Location: the declaration.\n- `diag.deprecated-use` — Summary: this item"
    " is deprecated. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.retired` `[Use-Deprecated]` (`spec/17` §1, D-0303"
    "). Invariant: none. Required: the name used is live. Observed: its declaration is marked `[[deprecat"
    "ed(\"m\")]]`, or its module's or its type's is. Provenance: the use, and the declaration that carries "
    "the attribute. Repair: write what the message says instead; meanwhile `--allow-deprecated` accepts t"
    "he program and reports each use as a warning. Related: `ex.deprecated-use`.\n- `diag.removed-use` —"
    " Summary: this item was removed. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.retired` `[Use-Removed]` (`spec/1"
    "7` §1, D-0303). Invariant: none. Required: the name used is live or deprecated. Observed: it is a t"
    "ombstone, `[[removed(\"m\")]]`, or its module or its type is. Provenance: the use, and the tombstone. "
    "Repair: write what the message says instead; no flag accepts a removed name. Related: `ex.removed-us"
    "e`.\n- `diag.unittest-name` — Summary: this test's name cannot be used. Phase: static. Rule: `rule."
    "module.unittest` `[Unittest-Name]` (`spec/17` §6, D-0230). Invariant: none. Required: a `unittest`'"
    "s name, when it has one, is not empty, holds no control character, and is not the name of another te"
    "st of the same module. Observed: an empty name, a control character, or a second test of the module "
    "with that name. Provenance: the test and, for a repeated name, the first test with it. Repair: name "
    "each test of a module differently, say what it checks, or leave the name out. Location: the name.\n- "
    "`diag.type-annotation-needed` — Summary: the compiler cannot take a generic call's or variant's ty"
    "pe arguments from what is written. Phase: static (reported by `cobc` while it lowers the program). R"
    "ule: `rule.type.expected` (reports 409, 410, 411, D-0339). Invariant: none. Required: each type argu"
    "ment is fixed by an argument, the expected type or an explicit annotation. Observed: an `auto` bindi"
    "ng, array or argument whose `Ok`, `Err`, `Some`, `None` or generic call leaves one open where `cobc`"
    " lowers it. Provenance: the expression. Repair: write the type where the value is declared (`Result<"
    "u8, str> r = …;`) or give the call or variant its types (`Ok<u8, str>(…)`). Location: the functi"
    "on and line.\n- `diag.type-mismatch` — Summary: the types do not match. Phase: static. Rule: `rule."
    "type.typing` (any `[T-*]` premise failing), `[T-Convert]`, `[T-Alt]`, `[Limits-Not-Number]`, `[Print"
    "-Not-Printable]`, `[Append-Not-Printable]`, `[Parse-Not-Numeric]`, `[Format-Arg-Mismatch]`, `[Key-No"
    "t-Hashable]`, `[Foreach-Not-Iterable]`, `[Foreach-Range-Ill-Typed]`, `[Let-Destructure-Fields]`, `[A"
    "rray-Repeat-Not-Plain]`. Required: the operand types the rule names. Observed: a different type. Pro"
    "venance: each operand's declaration or synthesis site. Repair: convert explicitly (`rule.arith.conve"
    "rt`) or fix the types.\n- `diag.unbounded-type-parameter` — Summary: the type parameter's bound doe"
    "s not allow this. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.type.kind`, `rule.type.bound` `[Bound-Missing]`. Requir"
    "ed: only the permitted uses of `T`, and the operators its bound provides. Observed: an operator its "
    "bound (if any) does not provide, field access, or call on `T`. Provenance: the generic declaration. "
    "Repair: give `T` the bound the operator needs (`<T: eq>` for `==`, `<T: ordered>` for `<`, `<T: numb"
    "er>` for `+`, D-0090), or pass the operation in as a `fn` parameter.\n- `diag.cannot-infer-type-param"
    "eter` — Summary: a type argument cannot be inferred here. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn.generic-ca"
    "ll` `[Generic-Call-Uninferable]`, `rule.arith.limits` `[Limits-Uninferable]`. Required: every type p"
    "arameter determined by an argument or the expected type. Observed: one is not. Provenance: the argum"
    "ent list and enclosing annotation, both lacking it. Repair: `name<τ>(…)` or annotate the declarat"
    "ion. Related: `ex.generic-box`.\n- `diag.instantiation-unbounded` — Summary: a generic function's i"
    "nstantiations do not end. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn.generic-call` `[Generic-Instantiation-Unboun"
    "ded]`. Required: a finite set of instantiations, each type argument nested at most 64 deep and made "
    "of at most 4,096 type constructors, at most 100,000 in all; no generic type whose fields lead back t"
    "o it at a larger type argument (`spec/16` `[Type-Recursion-Expanding]`). Observed: an instantiation "
    "at a type argument nested deeper or larger (a function calling itself at a larger type: `f<T>` calli"
    "ng `f<Box<T>>`, or `f<Two<T>>` doubling it), more instantiations, or a type such as `Nest<T>` holdin"
    "g a `Nest<Option<T>>`. Provenance: the generic function's declaration. Repair: pass the larger value"
    " as a type the function already has (a `Vec`, a `Box` of one fixed type), or split the function.\n- `"
    "diag.break-outside-loop`, `diag.return-outside-fn` — Summary: `break` or `continue` outside a loop"
    ", or `return` outside a function, has nothing to leave here. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.control.whil"
    "e` / `rule.fn.return`. Required: lexically inside a `while` / function body. Repair: move the statem"
    "ent into the loop it is meant to leave; a `match` arm needs no `break`.\n- `diag.capture-list-mismatc"
    "h` — Summary: the capture list does not match the names the closure uses. Phase: static. Rule: `ru"
    "le.fn.closure` `[Closure-Capture-List-Rejected]`. Invariant: none (a well-formedness check on the cl"
    "osure literal, not a safety invariant). Required: the written capture list, as a set, equals the clo"
    "sure body's free variables. Observed: a name missing from the list, an extra name not used in the bo"
    "dy, or both. Provenance: the closure literal's `[...]` vs. a syntactic scan of its body. Repair: add"
    " the missing name(s) or remove the unused one(s); the list documents an already-derived fact, it can"
    "not select a different capture set. Related: `ex.closure-capture`.\n\n## Validity of access paths\n\n- `"
    "diag.stale-binding` — Summary: this value is no longer valid. Phase: both. Rule: `[Binding-Lookup-"
    "Stale]`, `[Read-Stale]`, `[Write-Stale]`, `[Borrow-Stale]`, `[Field-Access-Stale]`, `[Destroy-Stale]"
    "`, `[Fn-Value-Empty-Call]`. Invariant: `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: `temporally-valid(a)`. Obs"
    "erved: false. Provenance: the invalidating event (object end at frame exit, last holder ended, state"
    "ment end, transfer, relocation, buffer release, a `fn` value's closure moved out) vs. this use. Repa"
    "ir: use the current holder after a move, or give the binding a new value first (`x = e`, `spec/11` `"
    "[Assign-Reestablish]`); do not keep a reference past its referent's or its holder's scope; re-index "
    "after a `Vec` reallocation. Related: `ex.use-after-move`, `ex.double-destroy`.\n- `diag.use-of-uninit"
    "ialized` — Summary: this is used before it has a value. Phase: static (`rule.init.definite-assignm"
    "ent`, rejects on unknown); dynamic guard `[Read-Uninitialized]`, `[Write-Partial-Init]`. Invariant: "
    "`inv.initialization-validity`. Required: `init = valid` (a whole-object write on every path; no fiel"
    "d write into an uninitialized aggregate). Observed: a path without a write, or a projection write be"
    "fore the whole. Provenance: the CFG path from block entry. Repair: initialize on every path; initial"
    "ize aggregates whole. Related: `ex.definite-assignment`.\n- `diag.reference-escapes-scope` — Summar"
    "y: this reference would outlive what it refers to. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.temporal.ref-escape`, "
    "`rule.temporal.elision`. Invariant: `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: no use of the reference outsi"
    "de its referent's block. Observed: stored into an enclosing block's binding or returned. Provenance:"
    " `referent-block` vs. the escaping store. Repair: return an owned value, or restructure. Related: `e"
    "x.reference-escape`.\n- `diag.reference-identity` — Summary: a warning of `--check`: `==` or `!=` b"
    "etween two references to a type parameter bound `eq` (or `ordered`), which compares where they refer"
    ", not the values. Phase: static (a warning; the program is accepted). Rule: `spec/09` (reference equ"
    "ality is identity; report 346). Invariant: none. Required: nothing; the comparison is identity. Obse"
    "rved: `x == v` with `x`, `v` of type `ref<T, _>`, `T: eq`. Provenance: the comparison. Repair: `*x ="
    "= *v` for the values; `rawptr_of(x) == rawptr_of(v)` for the place. Location: the comparison.\n- `dia"
    "g.lifetime-elision-ambiguous` — Summary: it is not clear which parameter the returned reference co"
    "mes from. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.temporal.elision` `[Call-Multi-Ref-Return-Rejected]`. Required:"
    " a function returning a reference has exactly one reference parameter, and one returning a value tha"
    "t holds references at most one, or a `from` clause. Observed: a reference result with zero or severa"
    "l reference parameters, or a result that holds references (`Option<ref<T, shared>>`, `Vec<StringView"
    ">`, a struct with a reference field) with several (D-0319), and no clause. Provenance: the signature"
    ". Repair: with several reference parameters, name the ones the result may come from with `from p` or"
    " `from p, q` (D-0312, D-0318), or take the others by value; with none, return an owned value. Relate"
    "d: `ex.lifetime-elision`.\n- `diag.result-source-invalid` — Summary: this `from` clause names no so"
    "urce the result could come from. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.temporal.elision` `[Result-Source-Form]`"
    " (D-0312, D-0318). Required: each name in the clause is a parameter of reference type, named once, a"
    "nd the result's type may hold a reference. Observed: a name that is no parameter, a parameter of ano"
    "ther type, a name given twice, or a result that holds no reference. Provenance: the signature. Repai"
    "r: name the reference parameters the result is taken from, each once, or drop the clause.\n- `diag.pr"
    "econdition-failed` — Summary: a requirement of the called function does not hold. Phase: both. Rul"
    "e: `rule.fn.requires` `[Requires-Fail]` (`spec/15`, D-0317); statically, the requirement row of `spe"
    "c/14` §6. Invariant: none. Required: each requirement of the callee's `requires` block holds for th"
    "e call's arguments. Observed: one does not (its message, formatted, is shown after the location; wit"
    "h none, which requirement of which function). Provenance: the call. Repair: establish the condition "
    "before the call, or test it and take another path. Location: the call.\n- `diag.requires-misplaced` —"
    " Summary: this function cannot have a `requires` block. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn.requires` `[Re"
    "quires-Place]` (`spec/15`, D-0317). Required: a `requires` block stands on a function a program call"
    "s. Observed: on `main`, on a type's `drop`, or on a function C calls (`extern fn` with a body). Prov"
    "enance: the signature. Repair: check the condition in the body with `assert`, or in the caller.\n- `d"
    "iag.result-source-kept` — Summary: this keeps a reference parameter the `from` clause does not nam"
    "e. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.temporal.elision` `[Result-Source-Probe-Only]` (D-0312, D-0318). Invar"
    "iant: `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: every reference parameter the clause does not name is only "
    "probed: read for a value that holds no reference of it. Observed: an occurrence bound, stored, retur"
    "ned, captured, or passed where it could be kept. Provenance: the occurrence and the clause. Repair: "
    "read only what is needed from it (its length, a comparison, a search's position), or name it in the "
    "clause instead.\n\n## Aliasing\n\n- `diag.aliasing-conflict` — Summary: this access conflicts with a l"
    "ive reference. Phase: both. Rule: `[Borrow-Denied]`, `[Read-Conflict]`, `[Write-Conflict]`, `[Match-"
    "Conflict]`, `[Thread-Affine]` (D-0213: an exclusive path of another running thread), `[Thread-Lend]`"
    " (a second lend of a live lent path). Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`, `inv.concurrency-validity`. R"
    "equired: `¬clash(a, m)`. Observed: `witness(a, m, Σ)` — a live non-ancestor path with overlappin"
    "g target and incompatible mode. Provenance: the witness's formation event (which borrow, in which th"
    "read) vs. this access. Repair: end the conflicting reference (let its holder go out of scope) before"
    " this access, or use `shared` on both sides. Related: `ex.borrow-conflict`, `ex.projection-conflict`"
    ".\n- `diag.borrow-exceeds-source` — Summary: this reference would allow more than its source does. "
    "Phase: static; dynamic for `[Read-Fn-Through-Shared]`. Rule: `[Borrow-Exceeds-Source]`, `[T-Read-Thr"
    "ough-Shared]` (an exclusive reference read through a shared one, where an exclusive one is expected)"
    ", `[Read-Exclusive-Through-Shared]`, `[Match-Exclusive-Through-Shared]`, `[Read-Fn-Through-Shared]` "
    "(D-0218). Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`. Required: an exclusive borrow's source is exclusive; noth"
    "ing reached through a shared reference is used as a writer. Observed: source mode `shared`; a copy h"
    "olding an exclusive reference; a closure with an exclusive capture. Provenance: the source reference"
    "'s declared mode. Repair: take `ref<τ, exclusive>` where mutation is needed. Related: `ex.shared-is"
    "-read-only`.\n- `diag.write-through-shared` — Summary: this writes through a shared reference. Phas"
    "e: static. Rule: `[Write-Not-Exclusive]` (a place reached through a shared path, including through a"
    "n exclusive reference it holds: `[Read-Ref-Through-Shared]`, D-0218). Invariant: `inv.alias-validity"
    "`. Required: `mode(a) = exclusive`. Observed: `shared`. Provenance: the path's mode at formation. Re"
    "pair: take the reference as `ref<T, exclusive>` (and pass `&mut x`) where it is written through, or "
    "write to a value of your own. Related: `ex.shared-is-read-only`.\n- `diag.destroy-while-aliased` — "
    "Summary: this is destroyed while a reference to it is live. Phase: both. Rule: `[Destroy-Not-Solitar"
    "y]`. Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`, `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: `solitary(a)`. Observed: an"
    "other live path (a reference, a guard). Provenance: that path's formation. Repair: let the reference"
    "'s holder end first; release the guard. Related: `ex.destroy-while-borrowed`.\n- `diag.move-while-ali"
    "ased` — Summary: this is moved while a reference to it is live. Phase: both. Rule: `[Authority-Tra"
    "nsfer-Aliased]`, `[Relocate-In-Aliased]`, `[Rawptr-Move-In]`/`-Out]` premises. Invariant: `inv.alias"
    "-validity`. Required: no other live path on the moved object. Observed: one exists. Provenance: its "
    "formation. Repair: end the reference before moving. Related: `ex.move-while-borrowed`.\n- `diag.move-"
    "out-of-field` — Summary: a part of a live value cannot be moved out on its own. Phase: static. Rul"
    "e: `[Store-Binding-Place-Transfer-Sub]`, `[Destroy-Projection]`, `[Match-Move-Through-Ref]`, `[Let-D"
    "estructure-Destructor]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: a moved resource is a whole "
    "object. Observed: a field/element/payload of a live object, or a payload reached through a reference"
    ". Provenance: the projection. Repair: move the whole container, or take a reference to the field.\n- "
    "`diag.borrow-of-non-place`, `diag.borrow-of-temporary` — Summary: only a place can be borrowed. Ph"
    "ase: static. Rule: `[Ref-Form-Not-Place]`, `[Ref-Form-Temporary]`; `[Simd-Lane]` (`spec/16` §3b, D-"
    "0254). Required: the operand of `&` is a place rooted in a binding, reference, or reclaim. Observed:"
    " a value or a temporary; a bit field; a lane of a `simd`, or a range of them. Repair: bind it first;"
    " read or assign the lane, or borrow the whole vector.\n\n## Resource authority\n\n- `diag.no-destroy-aut"
    "hority` — Summary: this code no longer owns the value it destroys. Phase: both. Rule: `[Destroy-No"
    "-Authority]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: unconsumed authority in this thread. Ob"
    "served: absent (moved to another thread) or consumed. Provenance: the consuming/transferring event. "
    "Repair: destroy in the owning thread, once. (A second `drop(x)` through the same binding reports `di"
    "ag.stale-binding` first.) Related: `ex.double-destroy`.\n- `diag.transfer-without-authority` — Summ"
    "ary: this code no longer owns the value it hands on. Phase: both. Rule: `[Authority-Transfer-Unautho"
    "rized]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`, `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: a valid source hold"
    "ing authority. Observed: stale or unauthorized. Provenance: the earlier move/destroy. Repair: move f"
    "rom the current holder. Related: `ex.use-after-move`.\n- `diag.overwrite-of-live-resource` — Summar"
    "y: this overwrites a resource that has not been ended. Phase: both. Rule: `[Write-Resource-Overwrite"
    "-Rejected]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: the target holds no live resource, or it"
    "s type is quiet (D-0194: then the write destroys it). Observed: an outstanding obligation at the tar"
    "get. Provenance: the establishing/moving event that put it there. Repair: `overwrite(&mut place, v)`"
    " to put `v` there and destroy the old value (D-0080), `replace(&mut place, v)` to keep the old value"
    ", or `drop` the old value first. Related: `ex.no-silent-resource-overwrite`.\n- `diag.text-join` — "
    "Summary: `+` does not join text. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.type.typing` (`+` is arithmetic; D-0073,"
    " D-0337). Invariant: none. Required: number operands for `+`. Observed: an operand that is text (a `"
    "String`, a `str`, a `StringView`). Provenance: the operator. Repair: append to a `String` with `Stri"
    "ng::append(&mut s, t)` (text, a `str` or a number) or `String::appendf(&mut s, \"%s\", t)`, or build o"
    "ne with `sprintf(\"%s%s\", a, b)`. Location: the operator's expression.\n- `diag.read-of-resource` — "
    "Summary: a resource cannot be copied by reading it. Phase: static. Rule: `[Read-Resource-Rejected]`."
    " Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: `¬is-resource(type(a))` in value position. Observed"
    ": resource. Provenance: the type declaration. Repair: move it, or take a reference. Related: `ex.no-"
    "copy-of-resource`.\n- `diag.destructor-on-plain-type` — Summary: only a resource can have a destruc"
    "tor. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/07` §1 (D-0075). Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: a t"
    "ype with a destructor is a resource in every instantiation. Observed: `T::drop` declared for a type "
    "that is not one, or for an enum, which has no destructor (D-0336). Provenance: the destructor's decl"
    "aration. Repair: declare the type `resource struct T`; an enum has no destructor, so wrap it in a `r"
    "esource struct`.\n- `diag.bad-destructor-signature`, `diag.direct-destructor-call` — Summary: a des"
    "tructor must be `T::drop(ref<T, exclusive> self)`, called only by `drop`. Phase: static. Rule: `spec"
    "/07` §1. Required: `T::drop(ref<T, exclusive> self)`, invoked only by `[Destroy]`. Repair: fix the "
    "signature; use `drop(x)`.\n\n## Arithmetic\n\n- `diag.arith-overflow` — Summary: arithmetic overflow. "
    "Phase: both. Rule: `[Arith-Checked-Overflow]`, `[Neg-Overflow]`. Invariant: `inv.arith.range-validit"
    "y`. Required: `r ∈ represented-domain(τ)`. Observed: outside. Provenance: the operand values at t"
    "his expression. Repair: widen, or use `wrapping_`/`saturating_`/`checked_`. Related: `ex.checked-ari"
    "thmetic`, `ex.negation`.\n- `diag.div-by-zero` — Summary: division by zero. Phase: both. Rule: `[Di"
    "v-By-Zero]`. Required: `v2 ≠ 0`. Repair: test first, or `checked_div`. Related: `ex.checked-arithm"
    "etic`.\n- `diag.div-overflow` — Summary: division overflow: the minimum divided by -1. Phase: both."
    " Rule: `[Div-Overflow]`. Required: `¬(v1 = min(τ) ∧ v2 = -1)`. Repair: `checked_div` or widen. R"
    "elated: `ex.checked-arithmetic`.\n- `diag.shift-amount-out-of-range` — Summary: shift amount out of"
    " range for the type. Phase: both. Rule: `[Shift-Amount-Invalid]`. Required: `0 ≤ n < bitwidth(τ)`"
    ". Repair: mask the amount.\n- `diag.narrowing-overflow` — Summary: the value does not fit the narro"
    "wer type. Phase: both. Rule: `[Narrow-Overflow]`, `[Float-To-Int-Invalid]`, `[Bitfield-Overflow]` (`"
    "spec/16` §2a, D-0118). Required: `v ∈ represented-domain(τ')`. Repair: `narrow_wrapping` or a wi"
    "der target for an integer; for a float (`to_int`), test its range first.\n- `diag.literal-out-of-rang"
    "e` — Summary: this literal does not fit its type. Phase: static. Rule: `[Literal-Out-Of-Range]`. R"
    "equired: `val(L) ∈ represented-domain(τ)`; for a float literal, that it does not round beyond `τ"
    "`'s largest finite magnitude. Provenance: the literal vs. its determined type. Repair: fix the liter"
    "al or annotation.\n\n## Aggregates\n\n- `diag.recursive-type` — Summary: this type contains itself. Ph"
    "ase: static. Rule: `rule.agg.layout` `[Type-Recursive]` (`spec/16` §1). Invariant: none. Required: "
    "no struct or enum contains itself by value. Observed: a chain of fields, payloads, array elements or"
    " `mutex` values leading back to the type, with no pointer on the way. Provenance: the type's declara"
    "tion. Repair: put the recursive part behind a `Box<T>` (one owner), an `Rc<T>` (shared) or a `Vec<T>"
    "` (many). Location: the declaration.\n- `diag.static-assert-failed` — Summary: static assertion fai"
    "led. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.static-assert` `[Static-Assert-Failed]` (`spec/17` §1). Inva"
    "riant: none. Required: the condition of `static_assert` is `true`. Observed: `false`, for the progra"
    "m as written or for one instantiation of a generic function (the message given, if any, is shown, fo"
    "rmatted with its arguments' values). Provenance: the assertion and the constants and types it names."
    " Repair: fix what the assertion guards, or the assertion. Location: the assertion.\n- `diag.static-as"
    "sert-not-constant` — Summary: a static assertion's condition must be known before the program runs"
    ". Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.static-assert` `[Static-Assert-Not-Constant]` (`spec/17` §1b). "
    "Invariant: none. Required: the condition of `static_assert` is a `bool` constant expression — lite"
    "rals, constants (module or local), operators, `sizeof`, `alignof`, the limits and the conversions —"
    " so that it can be computed before the program runs. Observed: the condition (or an argument of its "
    "message) names a local variable or parameter, calls a function or reads a container, or the conditio"
    "n is not a `bool`. Provenance: the condition. Repair: for a condition that is only known when the pr"
    "ogram runs, use `assert` (`spec/18` §1a); to check a value before the program runs, name it with `c"
    "onst` (a local `const` works: `const u8 D = B + 1;`). Location: the assertion.\n- `diag.not-char-boun"
    "dary` — Summary: this bound falls inside a character. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.stringvie"
    "w` `[View-Boundary]` (`spec/21` §2h). Invariant: `inv.string.utf8-validity`. Required: both bounds "
    "of a `StringView` fall at the start of a character or at the end of the text. Observed: a bound insi"
    "de a character's UTF-8 encoding. Provenance: the view's bounds. Repair: move the bound to a characte"
    "r's start (a byte that is not `0b10xxxxxx`), for example by searching with `StringView::find`. Locat"
    "ion: the view.\n- `diag.invalid-datetime` — Summary: this date and time do not exist. Phase: dynami"
    "c. Rule: `rule.stdlib.time` `[Invalid-DateTime]` (`spec/21` §2j, D-0140). Invariant: none. Required"
    ": the `DateTime` names a moment of the proleptic Gregorian calendar (a month 1 to 12, a day within i"
    "ts month, an hour below 24, a minute and a second below 60) at most `i64` seconds from 1970. Observe"
    "d: a field out of range, or a year too far from 1970. Provenance: the `DateTime`, written as a struc"
    "t literal or with its fields changed. Repair: make it with `DateTime::new`, which returns `None` for"
    " such fields, or with `DateTime::from_unix`/`from_iso`. Location: the call of `DateTime::to_unix` (o"
    "r `weekday`).\n- `diag.entropy-unavailable` — Summary: the operating system gave no secure random b"
    "ytes. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §0 `[Os-Random]` (D-0142). Invariant: none. Required: the ope"
    "rating system gives bytes from its cryptographically secure source. Observed: it has none, or refuse"
    "d (on Linux, no `getrandom` and no readable `/dev/urandom`, as in a bare container). Provenance: the"
    " call. Repair: run where the system provides secure randomness; never substitute a clock or a fixed "
    "seed for keys. Location: the call of `os_random_bytes`, `os_random_u64` or `Rng::from_os`.\n- `diag.h"
    "kdf-length` — Summary: HKDF cannot produce more than 8160 bytes. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §"
    "2m `[Hkdf]` (D-0152). Invariant: none. Required: `hkdf_expand`'s `len` is at most 8160, 255 blocks o"
    "f 32 bytes (RFC 5869's bound). Observed: a larger `len`. Provenance: the call. Repair: derive at mos"
    "t 8160 bytes from one pseudorandom key; derive more keys with different `info`. Location: the call o"
    "f `hkdf_expand` or `hkdf_sha256`.\n- `diag.crypto-length` — Summary: a key, nonce or digest of the "
    "wrong length. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §2m `[Crypto-Length]` (D-0153, D-0154, D-0165, D-0167"
    ", D-0168, D-0169, D-0170). Invariant: none. Required: a ChaCha20 or AEAD key of 32 bytes and a nonce"
    " of 12, an AES key of 16, 24 or 32 bytes and an AES-GCM nonce of 12 (D-0165), an X25519, P-256 or Ed"
    "25519 private key of 32 bytes and a P-384 private key of 48, a Poly1305 key of 32 bytes, a ChaCha20 "
    "message that fits in the 2^32 blocks after its starting counter, a BLAKE2b digest of 1 to 64 bytes u"
    "nder a key of at most 64, an RSA digest of its hash's length and a modulus long enough for the signa"
    "ture encoding, and an RSA key size of 1024 to 8192 bits in a multiple of 64. Observed: another lengt"
    "h. Provenance: the call. Repair: pass keys and nonces of the algorithm's sizes (a key from `hkdf_exp"
    "and` with `len` 32, a nonce of 12 bytes, a digest from `hash` of the `HashKind` named). Location: th"
    "e call into `std::crypto`.\n- `diag.kdf-parameters` — Summary: the key-derivation parameters are ou"
    "t of range. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §2m `[Kdf-Parameters]` (D-0170). Invariant: none. Requi"
    "red: `pbkdf2` runs at least one iteration; `argon2id` (and a PHC string `verify_password` reads, whi"
    "ch is false instead) has at least one pass, 1 to 255 lanes, at least 8 KiB of memory per lane, a sal"
    "t of at least 8 bytes and a result of at least 4 bytes (RFC 9106 §3.1). Observed: a parameter outsi"
    "de those bounds. Provenance: the call. Repair: pass the parameters the standard allows; `hash_passwo"
    "rd` chooses them itself. Location: the call of `pbkdf2` or `argon2id`.\n- `diag.not-ascii` — Summar"
    "y: this byte is not ASCII. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.text` `[Push-Ascii-Not-Ascii]` (`spec/"
    "21` §2d). Invariant: `inv.string.utf8-validity`. Required: the byte given to `String::push_ascii` i"
    "s below 128. Observed: a byte of 128 or more, which is not UTF-8 on its own. Provenance: the call. R"
    "epair: build bytes in a `Vec<u8>` and check them with `String::from_utf8`. Location: the call.\n- `di"
    "ag.index-out-of-bounds` — Summary: index out of bounds. Phase: both. Rule: `[Index-Out-Of-Bounds]`"
    ", `[Slice-Out-Of-Bounds]` (`spec/16` §3a), `spec/21` §1 `fault`, `[Str-Byte-Out-Of-Bounds]` (`spec"
    "/21` §2a), `arg`'s `fault` (`spec/21` §2c). Invariant: `inv.spatial-validity`. Required: `0 ≤ n "
    "< N` / `i < len` / `i < str_len(s)` / `i < arg_count()`. Observed: violated. Provenance: the index v"
    "alue vs. the fixed `N`, current `len`, the `str`'s byte count, or the number of arguments. Repair: c"
    "heck the index first (`i < Vec::len(&v)`, `i < slice_len(s)`), or take the last element out with `Ve"
    "c::pop(&mut v)`, an `Option`. Related: `ex.bounds-check`, `ex.str-literal`.\n- `diag.non-exhaustive-m"
    "atch` — Summary: this `match` does not cover every value. Phase: static. Rule: `[Match-Non-Exhaust"
    "ive]`. Required: the arms together match every value (every variant, at every level a pattern descen"
    "ds to, or `_`). Observed: a pattern no arm matches, given as the message. Provenance: the enum decla"
    "rations vs. the arms. Repair: add an arm for the pattern named, or a `_` arm. Related: `ex.exhaustiv"
    "e-match`.\n- `diag.unreachable-arm` — Summary: this arm can never be reached. Phase: static. Rule: "
    "`[Match-Unreachable]`. Required: each arm matches some value no earlier arm matches (arms are tried "
    "in order). Observed: an arm every value of which an earlier arm takes. Provenance: the arm vs. the e"
    "arlier arms. Repair: remove the arm, or move it before the arm that takes its values.\n\n## Failure, c"
    "oncurrency, trust\n\n- `diag.propagate-outside-fallible-context` — Summary: `?` cannot be used in th"
    "is function. Phase: static. Rule: `[Propagate-Err-Mismatch]`, `[Propagate-Option-Mismatch]` (D-0130)"
    ". Required: the function returns `Result<_, E>` with matching `E` (for a `Result` operand), or an `O"
    "ption` (for an `Option` operand). Provenance: the declared return type vs. the `?` site. Repair: cha"
    "nge the return type, `Result::map_err`, `Option::ok_or(o, e)?` (an `Option` in a `Result`-returning "
    "function), or `match`.\n- `diag.spawn-borrow-closure` — Summary: a spawned thread needs a `move` cl"
    "osure. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.conc.spawn`. Required: a `fn` value, a `move` closure, or a closur"
    "e capturing nothing (`[]`). Repair: add `move`.\n- `diag.not-thread-safe` — Summary: this would tak"
    "e a value confined to one thread to another. Phase: both. Rule: `rule.conc.spawn` `[Thread-Confined]"
    "` (`spec/19` §1); at run time `rule.stdlib.rc` (`Rc::clone`, `Rc::get`, `Rc::downgrade`, `Rc::drop`"
    ", `Weak::upgrade`, `Weak::clone`, `Weak::drop`). Invariant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: no"
    " argument of `spawn`, no capture of the closure it runs (nor of a closure binding that closure is) a"
    "nd not the thread's result is or reaches a thread-confined type: `Rc`, `Weak`, or a type holding or "
    "referring to one; and, at run time, an `Rc` or `Weak` is used only in the thread that made its box, "
    "whatever type of closure or field carried it elsewhere. Observed: the first such argument, capture o"
    "r result, and the confined type it holds; at run time, the message `an Rc made in another thread`. P"
    "rovenance: the `spawn`; at run time, the call of the `Rc` or `Weak` operation. Repair: share the val"
    "ue across threads as `Arc<T>` (atomic counts), or as `ref<mutex<T>, shared>` lent to the thread. Loc"
    "ation: the `spawn`; at run time, the operation.\n- `diag.mutex-reentrant-lock` — Summary: this thre"
    "ad already holds the lock. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `[Lock-Reentrant]`. Invariant: `inv.concurrency-val"
    "idity`. Required: the thread does not already hold the lock. Provenance: the live guard. Repair: rel"
    "ease the guard first.\n- `diag.trusted-outside-unsafe` — Summary: this needs an `unsafe` block. Pha"
    "se: static. Rule: `[Unsafe-Rejected]`. Invariant: `inv.trust-transition`. Required: every trusted co"
    "nstruct inside `unsafe { }`. Provenance: the construct vs. the nearest enclosing `unsafe`. Repair: w"
    "rap in `unsafe` after verifying the asserted property. Related: `ex.unsafe-required`.\n- `diag.extern"
    "-variadic-without-ellipsis` — Summary: a C library function that takes a variable argument list is"
    " declared without `...`. Phase: static. Rule: `[Extern-Variadic-Without-Ellipsis]` (`spec/20`, repor"
    "t 228, D-0339). Invariant: none. Required: a declaration of one of the C library's variadic function"
    "s the implementation lists (the `printf` and `scanf` families, `open`, `fcntl`, `ioctl`, `syscall`, "
    "`execl`, `strfmon`, `error`, …) ends in `...` after its fixed parameters, as C declares it. Observ"
    "ed: a declaration that lists a call's arguments in place of `...` (the form D-0336 allowed). Provena"
    "nce: the declaration. Repair: declare the fixed parameters and then `...` (`unsafe extern fn snprint"
    "f(rawptr<u8> buf, usize n, rawptr<u8> fmt, ...) : i32;`). Location: the declaration.\n- `diag.extern-"
    "non-ffi-type` — Summary: this type cannot cross into C. Phase: static. Rule: `[Extern-Non-Ffi-Type"
    "]`, `[Extern-Call-Variadic-Arg]`. Required: `FfiType` parameters and result: integers, `f32`, `f64`,"
    " `bool`, `void` (a result), `rawptr<τ>`, and plain structs of those (`ffi-struct`, D-0252); the sam"
    "e types, `void` apart, for each argument after a variadic C function's fixed parameters (`...`, repo"
    "rt 228). Observed: the first type that is none of these, named through the field path that reaches i"
    "t. Repair: pass `rawptr`/scalars, or a struct without resources, enums or bitstructs.\n- `diag.null-p"
    "ointer` — Summary: C's `NULL` where an address was required. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.ff"
    "i` `[From-C-Null]` (`spec/21` §3f, D-0252). Invariant: none. Required: the `rawptr` given to `Strin"
    "g::from_c`, `Vec::from_c_bytes`, `Vec::from_raw` (with elements to copy) or `copy_to_raw` (with a sl"
    "ice that is not empty) is not null; the message names the function. Observed: address 0. Provenance:"
    " the C function that returned it. Repair: test with `is_null` first; C functions return `NULL` for \""
    "none\". Location: the call.\n- `diag.assert-failed` — Summary: assertion failed. Phase: dynamic. Rul"
    "e: `rule.fail.assert` `[Assert-Fail]` (`spec/18` §1a). Invariant: none. Required: the condition of "
    "`assert` is `true`. Observed: `false` (the message the program gave, if any, formatted, is shown aft"
    "er the location). D-0322: when the condition compares two values of an integer type, `f32`, `f64` or"
    " `bool`, outside a generic function, the message also shows both: `assertion failed: 7 == 8`, or the"
    " program's message followed by `(7 == 8)`; a condition `p && q` is tested term by term. Provenance: "
    "the call. Repair: the program's own condition names what was assumed; find why it did not hold. Loca"
    "tion: the call.\n- `diag.channel-zero-capacity` — Summary: a channel needs a capacity of at least 1"
    ". Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.channel` `[Channel-Zero-Capacity]` (`spec/19` §3). Invariant: no"
    "ne. Required: the capacity given to `Channel::new` is at least 1. Observed: 0. Provenance: the call."
    " Repair: give the number of values the channel may hold; 1 for a hand-over. Location: the call.\n- `d"
    "iag.barrier-zero-parties` — Summary: a barrier needs at least one party. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `ru"
    "le.stdlib.waiting` `[Barrier-Zero-Parties]` (`spec/21` §3c‴). Invariant: none. Required: the numb"
    "er of parties given to `Barrier::new` is at least 1. Observed: 0. Provenance: the call. Repair: give"
    " the number of threads that meet at the barrier. Location: the call.\n- `diag.channel-deadlock` — S"
    "ummary: the only running thread waits on a channel nothing else can change. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `r"
    "ule.conc.channel` `[Channel-Deadlock]` (`spec/19` §3). Invariant: none. Required: while `Channel::s"
    "end` or `Channel::recv` waits, another thread exists that could change the channel. Observed: the pr"
    "ogram's only running thread waits on a full or empty channel that is not closed. Provenance: the cal"
    "l. Repair: send or receive from another thread, or `close` the channel before receiving the last val"
    "ue. Location: the call.\n- `diag.thread-cancelled` — Summary: this thread was cancelled. Phase: dyn"
    "amic. Rule: `rule.conc.cancel` `[Cancel]` (`spec/19` §1, D-0204). Invariant: none. Required: the th"
    "read was not asked to stop while it waits. Observed: `cancel` was called on its handle; it was waiti"
    "ng (a join, a lock, a channel, sleeping, a socket) or began to. Provenance: the `cancel` call. Repai"
    "r: none is needed when the stop was meant: the thread's failure is contained, and its joiner or hand"
    "le sees it; to let a thread finish, do not cancel it. Location: the wait.\n- `diag.mutex-poisoned` —"
    " Summary: a thread failed while holding this lock. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.lock` `[Lock-Poi"
    "soned]` (`spec/19` §2, D-0204). Invariant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: the mutex was not "
    "held by a thread whose fault was contained. Observed: such a thread held it when it failed, so its i"
    "nterior may be half-changed. Provenance: the failed thread's fault. Repair: find that fault (`try_jo"
    "in` gives it); keep a lock's block short, so that little can fail inside it. Location: the `lock`.\n-"
    " `diag.deadlock` — Summary: these threads would wait for each other forever. Phase: dynamic. Rule:"
    " `rule.conc.guarantee` `[Deadlock]` (`spec/19` §4, D-0204). Invariant: none. Required: the wait can"
    " end. Observed: waiting would close a cycle of threads waiting to join or lock each other's, or ever"
    "y thread waits on another, a mutex, a channel or an atomic (`Atomic::wait`, D-0253), and none on the"
    " clock or outside the program. When one thread alone waits on something other than a join or a lock "
    "(a semaphore, an atomic, a channel) and every other thread has ended or waits for it, the message sa"
    "ys so: \"`main` waits here forever: no other thread can end this wait\" (report 321). Provenance: the "
    "waits. Repair: take locks in one order; send before waiting to receive; store and notify before wait"
    "ing on an atomic another thread waits to see change; join a thread only after giving it what it wait"
    "s for. Location: the wait.\n- `diag.static-assigned` — Summary: a `static` is assigned or destroyed"
    ". Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.static` `[Static-Not-Assigned]` (`spec/17` §1a′, report 442, "
    "D-0339). Invariant: none. Required: a `static` lives as long as the program and is changed only thro"
    "ugh what it holds (an `Atomic`, a `mutex`). Observed: `S = e;` or `drop(S)` of a `static` `S`. Prove"
    "nance: the statement. Repair: change it through its interior (`Atomic::store(&S, x)`, `*lock(&S) = x"
    "`). Location: the assignment or the `drop`.\n- `diag.result-discarded` — Summary: a `Result` is dis"
    "carded. Phase: both. Rule: `spec/13` §3 `[Stmt-Result-Discarded]` (D-0099); a thread's `Result` los"
    "t with its handle, `spec/19` §1 `[Handle-Result-Lost]` (D-0340). Invariant: none. Required: a state"
    "ment's value that is a `Result` is used — propagated with `?`, matched, bound, passed or returned;"
    " a `handle<Result<…>>` is joined before it ends. Observed: an expression statement (or a block-lik"
    "e statement) whose value is a `Result`, discarded; a `handle<Result<…>>` binding that may reach it"
    "s scope's end unjoined; at run time, a handle that ended unjoined after its thread gave `Err`. Prove"
    "nance: the statement or the binding; at run time, the handle's end. Repair: handle the error (`?`, `"
    "match`), or discard the value on purpose with `_ = e;`.\n- `diag.thread-affine-moved` — Summary: a "
    "guard would be taken to another thread. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.conc.spawn` `[Thread-Confined]` ("
    "`spec/19` §1, D-0340). Invariant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: no argument of `spawn`, no "
    "capture of the closure it runs and not the thread's result is or holds a `guard<T>`: a guard stays o"
    "n the thread that locked it. Observed: the first such argument or capture, and the guard type. Prove"
    "nance: the `spawn`. Repair: pass `&m` (the mutex) and call `lock(m)` in the thread. Location: the `s"
    "pawn`.\n- `diag.never-returns` — Summary: a function declared `: never` can return. Phase: static. "
    "Rule: `spec/12` `[T-Never-Fn]` (D-0340). Invariant: none. Required: every path of a `: never` functi"
    "on's body ends in a `never` call (`exit`, another `: never` function) or a loop without `break`; it "
    "holds no `return`. Observed: a `return`, or a path that reaches the body's end. Provenance: the `ret"
    "urn`, or the body's last expression. Repair: end the path with `exit(…)` or another `: never` call"
    ". Location: the `return` or the function.\n- `diag.stack-exhausted` — Summary: calls nested too dee"
    "ply for the stack. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/15` §3 `[Call-Stack-Exhausted]` (D-0077). Invariant:"
    " none (an implementation limit). Required: the implementation can give the call a frame. Observed: c"
    "alls nested deeper than the stack the implementation provides. Provenance: the call. Repair: recurse"
    " less deeply (a loop, an explicit stack in a `Vec`).\n- `diag.unwrap-failed` — Summary: nothing to "
    "unwrap: `None` or `Err`. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §1 `Option::unwrap`, `Option::expect`, `Re"
    "sult::unwrap`, `Result::expect` (D-0082). Invariant: none. Required: the `Option` is `Some`, the `Re"
    "sult` is `Ok`. Observed: `None` or `Err` (`expect`'s message, or which call it was, is shown after t"
    "he location). Provenance: the call. Repair: match on the value, or give a default with `unwrap_or`, "
    "where its absence is possible. Location: the call.\n- `diag.alloc-failure` — Summary: memory could "
    "not be allocated. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §1/§3 `fault(alloc_failure)` after `allocate` re"
    "turns `Err`. Required: allocation succeeded. Provenance: the `allocate` call. Repair: none at the la"
    "nguage level; callers needing recovery call `allocate` themselves.\n\n## Change Log\n\n- 1.77.0 — `CHG"
    "-0483` (D-0340): new `diag.thread-affine-moved` and `diag.never-returns`; `diag.result-discarded` al"
